.TH "restoreAbort" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
restoreAbort \- abort Restore mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]db.restoreAbort()\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Sdb
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Cluster is set to Restore mode after restorePrepare() or an offline restore.
The user can abort Restore mode through this function.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
None
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, there is no return value.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When the exception happens，use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v5.0.2 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Abort Restore mode for the cluster.
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> db.restoreAbort()
\f[]
.fi
